// ------------------------------------------------------------------
// The Hyde Park walk. Thirteen stops on how the neighborhood was
// built and who it was built for, from Paul Cornell's stone at 53rd
// Street through the fair, the university, and the machinery of
// exclusion, closing the circle at the Obama Presidential Center,
// with two optional detours west along 63rd Street. The narration is
// written from the founder's family oral history (a recorded
// conversation outlining the tour), corrected and deepened against
// the sources listed on every stop; nothing in the transcript should
// outrun them. Key print source for the 2026 expansion: Susan
// O'Connor Davis, Chicago's Historic Hyde Park (University of
// Chicago Press, 2013), plus the documentary series The Shame of
// Chicago, Shame of the Nation. The six red plates are page-only and
// are not read into the audio. Audio is generated by
// scripts/walk-tts.mjs --tour hyde-park (OpenAI, voice ash);
// durations.json is the source of audioSeconds.
// ------------------------------------------------------------------

