        "The apartment tower on this corner opened in 1918 as the **Cooper-Carlton Hotel**. Look up and you can see carved faces in the terra cotta near the top, put there by owners who claimed a family line back to the novelist James Fenimore Cooper. In 1930 it took the name **Del Prado**, inherited from an older hotel out on the Midway that was being torn down to make room for International House.",
